<title>UK: INTERVIEW - Woolwich sees growth.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW - Woolwich sees growth.</headline>
<byline>Joe Ortiz</byline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Woolwich Building Society, which on Wednesday announced its last set of results before a planned stock market flotation, said it sees growth in all its businesses.</p>
<p>But Chief Executive John Stewart said that if draft building societies legislation is passed in its current form, the Woolwich would have to consider expansion by acquisition very carefully.</p>
<p>This is because in its current form the law would take away a building society's five-year immunity from takeover, which they enjoy under present legislation, if they take over another financial sector company.</p>
</text>
